{
  "_comment": "Keyless core MCP server set (owner directive decisions/agent-stack-v2-mcp-tools-and-profiles.md: tools come only from MCP servers). Copy to mcp.json (gitignored) and edit paths. Catalog, prerequisites (node 22+/npx, uv/uvx, Docker for the sandbox), trust notes and keyed integrations: configs/MCP.md and configs/mcp.integrations.json.example. Every version is PINNED and was checked on its registry 2026-11-05; the live MCP handshake has NOT been verified yet (pending owner approval, ticket T-20261105-curate-verify-and-pin-the-mcp-server-set). Tools are named mcp:<id>/<tool>; skills grant them by that name (skills/file-report uses mcp:filesystem/*).",
  "_comment_policy": "ADR-0139 D8 / ADR-0086: a tool with no `tools` entry and no `default_tool_policy` FAILS CLOSED (dangerous = approval required, effects read+write+egress). Servers that can write, send or execute list their read tools explicitly and carry NO default, so a tool added by a later server version arrives dangerous. Network reads declare `egress` but are not dangerous: no approval prompt, but the egress effect is visible to grants, profile allowlists and the egress auditor. `env` is a PASSTHROUGH list of variable NAMES the stdio child may inherit from the kernel environment (values are set in the kernel's environment, never here); CAMBRIAN_* and LANGFUSE_* never pass. WARNING: an empty `{\"mcp\": {}}` silently wipes any `mcp` block in config.json (Koanf merges per-key) - do not create mcp.json if you do not use MCP. On Windows, `npx`/`uvx`/`uv` resolve through PATHEXT; use forward slashes or escaped backslashes in paths. Each server carries `catalog_id`: the D8 sandbox takes its tier and sandbox declaration (egress) from that catalog entry; without it a server falls to the default third-party tier with no network, which Windows cannot enforce, and is refused (app/mcp_sandbox_test.go).",
  "mcp": {
    "default_session_budget": 0,
    "call_timeout_ms": 60000,
    "servers": [
      {
        "id": "fetch",
        "catalog_id": "fetch",
        "_note": "Official reference server (modelcontextprotocol/servers, MIT). Fetches a URL and returns Markdown. Network read: egress, no approval. It can reach localhost/intranet URLs - see MCP.md trust notes.",
        "transport": "stdio",
        "endpoint": "uvx",
        "args": [
          "mcp-server-fetch==2026.11.4"
        ],
        "auth": {
          "type": "none"
        },
        "tools": [
          {
            "name": "fetch",
            "dangerous": false,
            "effects": [
              "read",
              "egress"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "web-search",
        "catalog_id": "web-search",
        "_note": "Keyless DuckDuckGo search (nickclyde/duckduckgo-mcp-server, MIT, community). Rate-limited by DuckDuckGo; for production use a keyed provider (brave-search/tavily/exa) or self-hosted SearXNG from mcp.integrations.json.example.",
        "transport": "stdio",
        "endpoint": "uvx",
        "args": [
          "duckduckgo-mcp-server==0.7.0"
        ],
        "auth": {
          "type": "none"
        },
        "tools": [
          {
            "name": "search",
            "dangerous": false,
            "effects": [
              "read",
              "egress"
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "fetch_content",
            "dangerous": false,
            "effects": [
              "read",
              "egress"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "filesystem",
        "catalog_id": "filesystem",
        "_note": "Official reference server. ONLY the directories given as args are reachable - replace ./workspace with the absolute roots you want to expose. Pinned to 1.0.0 because 2.x declares node>=24 (2.2.0 is current). Write tools are dangerous.",
        "transport": "stdio",
        "endpoint": "npx",
        "args": [
          "-y",
          "@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem@1.0.0",
          "./workspace"
        ],
        "auth": {
          "type": "none"
        },
        "tools": [
          {
            "name": "read_text_file",
            "dangerous": false,
            "effects": [
              "read"
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "read_file",
            "dangerous": false,
            "effects": [
              "read"
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "read_media_file",
            "dangerous": false,
            "effects": [
              "read"
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "read_multiple_files",
            "dangerous": false,
            "effects": [
              "read"
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "list_directory",
            "dangerous": false,
            "effects": [
              "read"
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "list_directory_with_sizes",
            "dangerous": false,
            "effects": [
              "read"
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "directory_tree",
            "dangerous": false,
            "effects": [
              "read"
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "search_files",
            "dangerous": false,
            "effects": [
              "read"
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "get_file_info",
            "dangerous": false,
            "effects": [
              "read"
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "list_allowed_directories",
            "dangerous": false,
            "effects": [
              "read"
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "write_file",
            "dangerous": true,
            "effects": [
              "write"
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "edit_file",
            "dangerous": true,
            "effects": [
              "write"
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "append_file",
            "dangerous": true,
            "effects": [
              "write"
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "create_directory",
            "dangerous": true,
            "effects": [
              "write"
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "move_file",
            "dangerous": true,
            "effects": [
              "write"
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "copy_file",
            "dangerous": true,
            "effects": [
              "write"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "code-sandbox",
        "catalog_id": "code-sandbox",
        "_note": "Sandboxed code execution for data analysis: vndee/llm-sandbox (MIT) wrapped by tools/code_sandbox/server.py, launched from the kernel's directory (${CAMBRIAN_KERNEL_DIR}, kernel-provided). Hardened by env_values (network none, read-only root, no capabilities, no-new-privileges, 2g, 1 CPU) on the pre-built image SANDBOX_IMAGE (pandas, numpy, matplotlib, openpyxl; `make sandbox-image`). execute_code's `inputs` (ledger ids / the person's paths) are read by the kernel under the person's access and mounted read-only at /inputs for that run only; /outputs files come back as ledger entries. Needs Docker. SANDBOX_MOUNTS (a fixed read-only mount) is for tests and local development only.",
        "transport": "stdio",
        "endpoint": "uv",
        "args": [
          "run",
          "--no-project",
          "--directory",
          "${CAMBRIAN_KERNEL_DIR}",
          "--with",
          "llm-sandbox[mcp-docker]==0.3.46",
          "python",
          "tools/code_sandbox/server.py"
        ],
        "auth": {
          "type": "none"
        },
        "env": [
          "BACKEND",
          "DOCKER_HOST",
          "SANDBOX_NETWORK_MODE",
          "SANDBOX_READ_ONLY",
          "SANDBOX_CAP_DROP",
          "SANDBOX_SECURITY_OPT",
          "SANDBOX_MEMORY",
          "SANDBOX_CPU_COUNT",
          "SANDBOX_IMAGE"
        ],
        "tools": [
          {
            "name": "execute_code",
            "dangerous": true,
            "effects": [
              "read",
              "write",
              "egress"
            ],
            "staged_inputs": true
          },
          {
            "name": "get_supported_languages",
            "dangerous": false,
            "effects": [
              "read"
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "get_language_details",
            "dangerous": false,
            "effects": [
              "read"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "env_values": {
          "SANDBOX_IMAGE": "cambrian/code-sandbox:py311-1",
          "SANDBOX_NETWORK_MODE": "none",
          "SANDBOX_READ_ONLY": "true",
          "SANDBOX_CAP_DROP": "ALL",
          "SANDBOX_SECURITY_OPT": "no-new-privileges:true",
          "SANDBOX_MEMORY": "2g",
          "SANDBOX_CPU_COUNT": "1"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "shell",
        "catalog_id": "shell",
        "_note": "Replacement for the dead @cfdude/super-shell-mcp (npm 404). tumf/mcp-shell-server (MIT): runs ONLY executables named in ALLOW_COMMANDS (set it in the kernel environment, e.g. ALLOW_COMMANDS=git,ls,cat). It is NOT a sandbox: an allowed program runs with the kernel user's files, network and credentials. Always dangerous. Windows execution is unverified (developed for POSIX shells). VERIFIED 2026-11-05: does NOT run on Windows (imports the Unix-only `pwd` module); use it only on Linux/macOS deployments.",
        "transport": "stdio",
        "endpoint": "uvx",
        "args": [
          "mcp-shell-server==1.1.14"
        ],
        "auth": {
          "type": "none"
        },
        "env": [
          "ALLOW_COMMANDS",
          "ALLOW_PATTERNS"
        ],
        "tools": [
          {
            "name": "shell_execute",
            "dangerous": true,
            "effects": [
              "read",
              "write",
              "egress"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
